35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, it turns out a lot of people struggle to pay all at once! And some people didn't join because the yearly fee was too much!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It seems the atmosphere has shifted. Turnout dropped after we added charges to outings, and some members feel uneasy about the cost per visit.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"It's even worse than I thought. A tiny group of people are doing all the work and attending everything, while others barely show up.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The administrative burden is staggering. Chasing individual payments takes hours, and mid-year calculations are a nightmare for the treasurer.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Most of our costs are fixed, like the hall hire! Also, the old named-grade system caused a lot of friction and made people stop volunteering.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, if chasing money is that hard, maybe we should avoid any system that requires collecting fees at every single event?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Takumi, if only a few people are attending, perhaps a high flat fee is what's making the others hesitate to come out.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Kenji, if the costs are mostly fixed, then the people who come every day are basically subsidizing the ones who never show up.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, exactly. Any system that increases the number of transactions will likely lead to the next treasurer quitting.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, but we don't want to make it feel like a business! We need to keep it welcoming for the people who only come occasionally.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Jonathan, that's a good point. If we make it too expensive upfront, we lose the people who are already hesitant.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Kenji, I agree. We must be careful not to create a barrier that prevents our quieter members from feeling at home.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Kenji, welcoming is fine, but fairness is better. Why should the nine people doing all the setup pay the same as someone who never comes?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,We are caught between administrative ease and perceived fairness. We need a system that minimizes paperwork but doesn't alienate members.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, maybe there's a middle ground? I just don't want a system that feels rigid or creates ""grades"" of members again.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
